      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the maximum value for `CONFIG_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT_COUNT` for any board in the legacy code is 1.\n\nFurthermore, for the platforms that are using a dedicated charge port, most are setting `DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT \u003d\u003d CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT`.\n\nI think a better approach is to create `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT` as a boolean config.\n\nThen in this file, do the following assignment:\n```\n#undef CONFIG_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT_COUNT\n#ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT\n#define CONFIG_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT_COUNT\n#define DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT  CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT\n#endif\n```\n\nYou can reference bug b:229308304 which I created to track if more than one dedicated charge port needs support.",
